# Where the DeepSeek Harness installation lives on THIS machine.
#
# Copy this file to `.harness-root` and put the installation root on one line.
# The scripts read it when the argument and DSH_HARNESS_ROOT are absent, and it
# is the answer of last resort for a layout no standard location describes.
#
# `.harness-root` is git-ignored: it is machine state, never part of the project.
#
# With the desktop app, the root is the `resources/harness` directory inside the
# installation, for example:
#   <install-dir>\resources\harness
#   C:\Users\<you>\AppData\Local\Programs\<app>\resources\harness
#
# A valid root contains:
#   node_modules/@deepseek-ai/{cordis,dsh,dsh-tools}
#   node_modules/js-yaml
